  "review": [
    "No chorus field; 8/8/8/8. Ark/Noah idiom: תֵּבָה + סְפִינָה, מַעְיְנוֹת הַתְּהוֹם echoes Gen 7:11. Glossary: בַּלָּהָה for الأهوال, כִּבְשַׁן for أتون النار, שְׁטָר for شيك الغفران (a warrant/deed of pardon), גְּדוּדֵי הָרָע for قوات الشر, נִצָּחוֹן for النصرة. 2:5's \"cheque\" rendered as a legal warrant, not a loanword. Short 1:2/1:4/1:6/1:8 and 3:3/3:4 stay proportional to the Arabic. 3:7 keeps Nebuchadnezzar in the biblical spelling. Direct speech at 2:8 keeps the colon."
